NEED OF AN ARRAY :- 
-> suppose if i want to store more than one values of same data type I can't do that
   assigning to only one variable name like we used to do ex: " int num = 1,2 .... " XXXXXX (wrong)
-> then this array concept comes into the picture.
-> we can store same data typed values under one variable name assigned to in two ways
   1. int arr[] = {1,2,3,4}; where the [] telling its storing as a list of same data type
   2. int arr[] = new arr[4]; this is the case where we don't know the values but we knew
      that we have created an empty array of size 4.